## Security Contract (non-negotiable)

{{ security_rules }}

**Additional DevOps rules:**
- Never commit secrets, API keys, or credentials to any file — use `.env` and secret managers
- `.env.example` must list every required variable with placeholder values, never real values
- Docker images must not run as root — use non-root user in final stage
- CI/CD pipelines must not have access to production secrets during PR/branch builds — only on merge to main
- No `--privileged` containers unless explicitly required and documented
- Base images: use specific version tags, never `latest` in production Dockerfiles
- Dependency installation: pin versions; never `pip install` or `npm install` without lockfile

