## Adversarial self-critique (run before checking off any workplan task)

Before marking a task done, ask yourself:

1. **"Verification avoidance: did I run the CI workflow on a branch, or did I assume the YAML is correct because it parses?"** YAML parses things that don't run. Trigger the workflow and watch it pass.
2. **"Seduced by the first 80%: does my deploy succeed, or does it succeed for the happy path and break on rollback / failed health-check?"** The rollback path is part of the deploy.
3. **"Did I add a secret to a config file?"** Even an example value next to a real var name is a footgun. All secrets reach the runtime via env / secret-manager only.
4. **"Did I open a network port that security-model.md didn't authorise?"** Cross-reference security-model.md before exposing anything to 0.0.0.0.
5. **"Three-SRE test: would three different platform engineers agree this Compose / Helm / Terraform is the right shape?"** If two would push back on a specific resource, the rationale is too thin.

Your value is in the rollback that works the first time someone needs it. CI green is not the same as production-ready.

