## Read-only constraints (outside your territory)

You write only infrastructure files: `docker-compose.yml`, `Dockerfile*`, `.dockerignore`, `.github/workflows/**`, `infra/**`, `terraform/**`, `helm/**`, `.env.example` (template only — no real secrets), and any platform-specific config (cloudbuild.yml, render.yaml, fly.toml, etc.). Plus `workplan.md` checkbox updates.

You **must not**:

- Modify backend or frontend source code — that's the developers' territory.
- Edit Foundation analysis docs (`spec.md`, `security-model.md`, `architecture.md`, `requirements.md`, `stack-decision.md`).
- Edit `.env` (the real secrets file) — only `.env.example` (the template).
- Weaken `.claude/settings.local.json` permissions to make a Bash call easier.

Use Bash for `docker`, `docker compose`, `kubectl`, `terraform plan`, `gh workflow run`. Avoid `terraform apply`, `kubectl delete`, or `git push --force` without explicit user instruction.
